  "working_tree": "Uncommitted code-intelligence work; this receipt and documentation follow frozen checks.",
  "shared_implementation": "The shared resource interpreter retains Original(path) or Created(script ordinal) provenance through whole-tree forward and reverse moves. It chooses identity checks and intent/reconciliation/cleanup order once; descriptor-relative native identity and creation-receipt primitives serve both Remote and paired Local native workers.",
  "contract": [
    "Intelligence protocol 3 AnalysisContext now carries bounded opaque native identities aligned with its sorted file paths. The original affected-file aggregate binds these identities under the original service HMAC. Missing/link entries are empty. Archived omitted vectors preserve protocol-2 serialized identity and accepted recovery.",
    "Linux/macOS original fingerprints bind device/inode and optional birth time. Windows fingerprints bind native volume/file identity and creation time. Native review-bearing resource execution compares authenticated original identities at their current script locations; old records without such evidence keep their earlier checks.",
    "The shared interpreter retains original paths and creation ordinals for every object in moved subtrees. It checks originals, created objects and affected parents when reconciling steps, after durable active intent and before mutation, during retained inventory validation, and immediately before each retained-object cleanup.",
    "Created-object identity checks use the existing durable file anchors and directory creation receipts even after workspace and retained-location moves. Shared rollback preserves creation ordinals rather than deriving them from a changed cursor or path.",
    "Real original-LSP/HMAC verification under the physical gate and actual SQLite authority claim precede the accepted-recovery fixtures. Remote and original-proven paired Local workers accept unchanged originals after service shutdown, grant expiry and provider-setting invalidation, while preserving external same-byte replacements. Cases cover accepted Prepared state, an unacknowledged overwritten-directory transfer, irreversible cleanup and a replacement made after actual durable intent acknowledgement. They make no additional LSP action queries or command calls.",
    "Cleanup controls finish the durable decision without replaying the command or publishing the already-decided editor successor twice. Negative cleanup controls preserve the replacement and existing editor state.",
    "Created-tree tests cover unacknowledged workspace and private-retained moves, unchanged rollback and preservation of external same-byte child replacements. All native internal creation, journal-acknowledgement and inverse interruption contracts also pass.",
    "Physical folder current checks now verify the captured canonical path, leaf identity and ancestor identities. Reparenting a matching leaf behind a symlink or replacing its parent at the identical absolute path invalidates its old physical fence. Fresh capture establishes the new ancestry.",
    "Fresh installed workspace/command/interruption and declared-input workflows pass in both modes with rebuilt backend/frontend/native bundled artifacts. These production records still omit durable LanguageReview; native fixtures separately establish review-bearing identity behavior."
  ],
